<h1>Lemony Chicken and Orzo Soup</h1>
<h2>Ingredients</h2>
<ul>
<li>2 tablespoons olive oil</li>
<li>1 onion, diced</li>
<li>3 carrots, diced</li>
<li>4 cloves garlic, minced</li>
<li>8 cups low-sodium chicken broth</li>
<li>1 1/2 pounds boneless skinless chicken thighs</li>
<li>1 cup orzo</li>
<li>1 14.5-oz can cannellini beans, drained</li>
<li>1/2 teaspoon salt</li>
<li>1/4 teaspoon pepper</li>
<li>4 eggs</li>
<li>1/3 cup lemon juice</li>
<li>Zest of 1 lemon</li>
<li>1/4 cup parmesan, grated, plus more for serving</li>
<li>4 cups kale, de-ribbed and chopped</li>
<li>1 cup soft herbs (dill is best), chopped</li>
</ul>
<h2>Steps</h2>
<ol>
<li>Heat the olive oil in a dutch oven over medium-high heat.</li>
<li>Add the onion and carrots and cook, stirring often, until softened, about 4 minutes.</li>
<li>Add the garlic and cook for 30 seconds.</li>
<li>Add the chicken broth, chicken thighs, orzo, beans, salt, and pepper.</li>
<li>Bring to a boil, then reduce to a simmer and cook uncovered for 20 minutes.</li>
<li>Meanwhile, whisk the eggs, lemon juice, parmesan, and lemon zest in a large bowl until completely smooth, with no streaks of white.</li>
<li>Transfer the chicken to a cutting board. Move the pot off the heat and let the soup cool for 5 minutes. Shred the chicken with two forks, then chop into smaller pieces.</li>
<li>Whisking constantly, ladle 1/2 cup of the hot broth into the egg mixture, then whisk in 1 more cup.</li>
<li>Stir the tempered egg mixture into the soup. Add the kale and the chicken.</li>
<li>Cook over low heat until the soup thickens and the kale is tender.</li>
<li>Season with salt, pepper, and more lemon juice to taste.</li>
<li>Serve topped with the herbs and more parmesan.</li>
</ol>
